<title>

18 May 2021
Dear parent/carer
I am writing to inform you of an exciting opportunity for our current Year 11 students. In accordance
with the government guidelines, The Cowplain School will be offering a range of opportunities for
the continued development of our students from 7
th June through to 25th June.
We have developed a programme of bespoke workshops that are designed to offer guidance and
advice for our students, and to assist them in the next steps of their journey from secondary
education to adulthood. These workshops will be a mixture of online and in-school sessions and will
be hosted by The Cowplain School staff as well as select specialist providers.
Please do have a look through the attached programme of workshops. I hope you will agree there
are plenty of activities to further enrich our year eleven students before they say their final goodbye
to The Cowplain School.
Please do not hesitate to contact your child’s tutor if you have any questions regarding the activities
listed in the programme. Tutors will be happy to assist with booking specific sessions or providing
further information about individual sessions. If you already know what sessions you want to attend,
please see Mr Simmons to book.
Yours sincerely
Mrs van den Braak
Head of Upper School
